{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And they conspired against him to kill him</b> — They were planning to kill him by means of their devices, so that they would act cunningly against him before he drew near to them and would not need to shed his blood with their own hands. Thus they said in Bereshit Rabbah (Bereshit Rabbah 84:14): \"Let us set the dogs upon him.\" And perhaps they did so but did not succeed, and when they saw that he was drawing near to them and they could not kill him by their devices, they said one to another, \"Behold, this dreamer comes; and now let us kill him ourselves.\""], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:41:09.312812463Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}